lumns: Name, Department, Role, Start Date, and Status (Active/On Leave/Departed). Above the table there's a toolbar with: a search input, a dropdown to filter by department, a dropdown to filter by status, and a 'Download CSV' button. The table should have 8 rows of realistic employee data. Below the table, show 'Showing 8 of 42 employees' and pagination controls (Previous, page numbers 1-5, Next). Include a caption that describes the table.\n\nWrite the resulting HTML to `output/index.html` (or another file named in your task).\n\n```\n\n### faq-page/PROMPT.md\n\n```\n# faq-page\n\nCreate the HTML for a FAQ page for a SaaS product called 'FlowBoard'. The page should have: a page header with breadcrumb navigation (Home > Support > FAQ), a search/filter input to narrow down questions, 3 FAQ categories ('Getting Started', 'Billing & Plans', 'Integrations') each with 3-4 questions, and a 'Still need help?' section at the bottom with a link to contact support and a phone number. Questions should be expandable. Use realistic questions and short but helpful answers.\n\nWrite the resulting HTML to `output/index.html` (or another file named in your task).\n\n```\n\n### multi-step-form/PROMPT.md\n\n```\n# multi-step-form\n\nCreate the HTML for a multi-step checkout form for an online store. Step 1: Shipping information (full name, email, phone, street address, city, postal code, country dropdown). Step 2: Payment method (credit card with card number, expiry, CVV — just the fields, no actual processing). Step 3: Order review showing a summary of 2 items with quantities and a total. Each step should be clearly delineated. Include a progress indicator showing which step the user is on. Include proper error message markup for when a field is invalid, demonstrated on the email field.\n\nWrite the resulting HTML to `output/index.html` (or another file named in your task).\n\n```\n\n### pricing-comparison-table/PROMPT.md\n\n```\n# pricing-comparison-table\n\nCreate the HTML for a pricing page with 3 plan tiers: 'Starter' ($9/mo), 'Professional' ($29/mo), and 'Enterprise' (custom pricing). Show a comparison table of features across plans. Features: 'Projects' (5 / Unlimited / Unlimited), 'Storage' (10GB / 100GB / Unlimited), 'Team members' (1 / 10 / Unlimited), 'API access' (No / Yes / Yes), 'Priority support' (No / No / Yes), 'Custom integrations' (No / No / Yes). Each plan also has a CTA button ('Start Free Trial' for first two, 'Contact Sales' for Enterprise). The Professional plan should be highlighted as 'Most Popular'. Include a heading and a brief intro paragraph.\n\nWrite the resulting HTML to `output/index.html` (or another file named in your task).\n\n```\n\n### product-listing-page/PROMPT.md\n\n```\n# product-listing-page\n\nCreate the HTML for a product listing page. The page has a site header with logo and main navigation, a search bar, a sidebar with filter options (price range checkboxes, category checkboxes, an 'in stock only' toggle), and a main content area showing 6 product cards. Each card has an image, product name, price, a short description, and an 'Add to cart' button. There's also a footer with contact info and secondary nav links. Use realistic product names and prices — not 'Product 1'. The page title is 'Running Shoes — SportGear'.\n\nWrite the resulting HTML to `output/index.html` (or another file named in your task).\n\n```\n\n### settings-form-with-grouped-controls/PROMPT.md\n\n```\n# settings-form-with-grouped-controls\n\nCreate the HTML for an account settings page. It has sections for: 'Profile' (display name text input, bio textarea, avatar upload), 'Notifications' (email notifications toggle, push notifications toggle, notification frequency radio buttons: Instant/Daily Digest/Weekly Digest), 'Privacy' (profile visibility radio: Public/Friends Only/Private, checkboxes for 'Show online status' and 'Allow search engines to index my profile'), and a 'Danger Zone' section with a 'Delete Account' button that is visually distinct. Each section should be clearly grouped. Include a 'Save Changes' button at the bottom.\n\nWrite the resulting HTML to `output/index.html` (or another file named in your task).\n\n```\n\nReference files:\n(none)\n\nSkill files:\n(none)\n\nProduce the concrete eval output files. Do not score your own work.\nReturn only well-formed JSON with this shape. Do not include markdown, code fences, prose, or XML tags:\n```json\n{\n  \"output_files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"RESULT.md\",\n      \"contents\": \"The concrete output produced for this eval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nEach output_files path must be relative to the eval output directory."
